
  The plan is in [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/plans/2026-10-02-deploys-page.md[39m. I haven't changed any code, and nothing is committed
  ([38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/[39m is gitignored in this repo anyway). I'll wait for you to read it before starting.

  [1mMain decision: the page uses the component library.[0m [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m already has what the spec needs:
  - [38;5;153mdataTable[39m sorts rows and builds the sort links in the headers.
  - [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m + [38;5;153mselectField[39m give the dropdown that submits on change and carries the current sort along.
  - [38;5;153mstatusChip[39m has tones whose colors match the spec: green, red, amber, blue.
  - [38;5;153memptyState[39m and [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m cover the empty message and the header.

  The services page builds all of this by hand with its own table, select and [38;5;153m.pill[39m classes, so the plan tells the
  implementer not to copy it. No edits to [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m or the CSS are needed.

  [1mTwo tasks:[0m
  1. [1mPage renderer:[0m [38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m, with 14 rendering tests covering the filter, both sorts, the chips, durations,
     the empty state, the fallbacks for unknown query values, and escaping.
  2. [1mRoute and nav link:[0m one entry in [38;5;153mROUTES[39m and one in [38;5;153mNAV[39m, plus server tests for the 200 page and the 503. The 503
     reuses the existing "Snapshot unavailable" path.

  [1mChoices the spec left open[0m (listed in the plan under "Decisions the spec leaves open"; worth a look):
  - An unknown [38;5;153msort[39m resets to the default, newest first, and ignores any [38;5;153mdir[39m that came with it.
  - An unknown [38;5;153mdir[39m uses the column's starting direction: Service starts A→Z, Started starts newest first.
  - Clicking an inactive header sorts ascending. That's how [38;5;153mdataTable[39m already works, so from the default view, clicking
    "Started" shows oldest first.
  - Under the Service sort, deploys of the same service stay newest first.
  - With "All environments" selected and no deploys at all, the page says "No deploys".
  - Durations of an hour or more stay in minutes, e.g. "75m 0s", as the spec says.

